==Enemy==
Angelic Gory is essentially a souped-up [[Gory Dark]], with even higher health, DPS and speed, fewer knockbacks and a harder-to-counter trait.

==Strategy==
A good strategy for this enemy is to stall him with defensive cats like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]]/[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and strike him with mid-ranged cats such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. This will knock him back fairly easily, allowing for a quick breather for your team. [[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Dioramos]] also gets a chance to be useful against Angelic Gory, but be wary that he doesn't get swarmed too quickly!

[[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]] might not be the best choice against Angelic Gory, as her long attack animation causes her to miss often with Angelic Gory's high knockback count. If you have any [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Delivery Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] they also have a chance to prove their worth; as when supported by groups of [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cats]], they will effectively stall and destroy Angelic Gory as well as any Angelic support he may have.

